# Playful visual language & Lucide

Play on the surface, rigor underneath. UI = friendly **creative workshop / adventure lesson map** — not SaaS, not Anki, not XP farm.

## Icons

- Use **`lucide-react`** for all UI icons; no emoji as primary controls/nav.
- Nav metaphors: `Home`, `Map`, `Dumbbell`/`Sparkles`, `Trophy`/`Compass`; stash `BookmarkPlus`; packs `PackageOpen`; clear `Crown`; hints `CircleHelp`/`Lightbulb`; media `Volume2`/`Mic`; chrome `Undo2`/`Redo2`/`Pause`/`Play`.
- `strokeWidth={2}`–`2.5`; touch targets ≥ 44px; bottom nav = icon + label.

## Reference → UI (reinforce always)

| Reference | Do this |
|---|---|
| Yellow grid blueprint | Session/Journey ground = grid paper atmosphere |
| Orange game-screen frame | Chunky framed example/preview when showing “the thing in play” |
| Speech bubble + Why not!/Nah… | `GuideBubble` + striped cyan primary / simpler secondary |
| Winding numbered path | Adventure `PathMap`; active = cyan double-outline |
| Sunburst + yellow split lesson | Journey/header energy |
| Guide peering tab | Persistent guide personality, not a buried help link |
| Mint “Game Complete!” | Session clear celebration |
| Purple “All Clear!” + crown | Major checkpoint only — don’t paint the whole app dark-neon |
| Skyrim constellations | Progress secondary only; Home stays Continue hero |

## Color, shape, type

- Saturated yellow / orange / cyan (active) / magenta accents / mint success.
- Never flat single-fill chrome; prefer grid, sunburst, or celebration field.
- Large radii, **thick soft outlines**, chunky nodes/frames.
- Expressive display font; no Inter/Roboto/Arial/system as brand face.
- Avoid: purple-on-white SaaS, cream+terracotta, broadsheet hairlines, dark-mode-first default, glow everywhere.

## Screen rules

- **Home:** one composition, one loud Continue CTA; soft rows (comeback, stash) secondary.
- **Journey/Session:** path + guide + Confirm/Back; bridge activities — no skill-module menu ping-pong.
- **Progress:** “I can…” first; constellation optional.
- **Clear:** full-bleed celebratory moment, then Home.
- **Stash/Import:** same playful sheet language (“Stash it”, “Pack aboard”) — not admin forms.

## Playfulness checklist (every major screen)

1. Atmosphere (grid / sunburst / celebration)
2. One expressive element (guide, path, frame, or crown)
3. One recommended action visually loudest
4. Coach/game-show copy, still clear
5. Intentional motion on advance/success/clear (respect reduced-motion)

## Do / don’t

```tsx
// ✅
import { Home, Map, Crown, BookmarkPlus } from 'lucide-react'

// ❌
<button>🏠</button>
```

- ✅ Reward session clear, ability unlocks, real use / stash lock-in.
- ❌ XP per tap; punitive streaks; card-grid heroes; flat gray empty states.
